---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Three designers, one rectangle" hint="Three people edit the same rectangle for 12 seconds: 120 edits, each changing one property. Change who decides conflicts, what a screen does with changes that arrive while its own is unconfirmed, how slow the network is, and what happens when one person goes offline. The same edits are replayed every time.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>With the defaults (<b>Property by property</b>, <b>Keep my unconfirmed edit</b>, delay <b>100</b> ms, <b>30</b>% on the shared property, offline <b>never</b>) <b>19</b> of the <b>120</b> edits are overwritten, there are no flickers, and all three copies are identical at the end.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then set the shared-property slider to <b>0</b>: no edit is overwritten, because edits to different properties never conflict.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then set <b>Client screen</b> to <b>Show every server change</b>: each screen jumps back <b>20</b> times while its own edit waits. Set the delay to <b>300</b> ms and it jumps <b>118</b> times. The copies still end identical: flicker is only cosmetic.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then set <b>Who decides conflicts</b> to <b>Whole object</b>: every edit sends all four properties, so <b>119</b> of the <b>120</b> edits are overwritten, even though most people touch different properties.</li>
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>, then set <b>Client C offline</b> to <b>6</b> s: <b>20</b> edits are made offline and replayed after a fresh copy is downloaded.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg fmp" data-fmp>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Who decides conflicts <select class="pg-in" data-rule><option value="prop">Property by property</option><option value="whole">Whole object</option></select></label>
      <label>Client screen <select class="pg-in" data-screen><option value="keep">Keep my unconfirmed edit</option><option value="naive">Show every server change</option></select></label>
      <RangeField label="One-way network delay (ms)" name="d" min="10" max="500" step="10" value="100" />
      <RangeField label="Edits to the shared property (%)" name="o" min="0" max="100" step="10" value="30" />
      <RangeField label="Client C offline (s)" name="f" min="0" max="15" value="0" />
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Edits overwritten</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Screen flickers</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Copies at the end</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Edits made offline</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <table class="fmp-table">
      <caption class="pg-note">The edit that holds each property at the end: its number and who made it.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Property</th><th scope="col">Server</th><th scope="col">A</th><th scope="col">B</th><th scope="col">C</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody data-rows></tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model, invented for teaching and not Figma data: three clients A, B and C take turns making one edit every 100 ms or so, 120 edits in all. A edits the property x, B edits y and C edits width, except that each edit goes to the shared property fill with the chance you set. Network delay is the one-way time between a client and the server, with a little random spread, and each connection keeps its order. The server handles changes in the order they arrive and sends each to all three clients, which is also the sender's confirmation. With the whole-object rule an edit carries the sender's copy of all four properties, so it also puts back any value the sender had not yet seen change. An edit is counted as overwritten when a later change replaced it without its author having seen it. A screen flicker is a time when a screen showed another person's value, or an older value of its own, over an edit of its own that was still unconfirmed. When Client C goes offline at 3 s it keeps editing on its own copy; on reconnecting it downloads the server's current state and then replays its queued edits, as Figma's 2019 post describes.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style>
  .fmp-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0; font: .82rem var(--font-mono); }
  .fmp-table caption { text-align: left; padding-bottom: 6px; }
  .fmp-table th, .fmp-table td { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 4px 6px; text-align: left; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .fmp-table thead th { background: var(--surface); }
</style>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fmp]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const PROPS = ['x', 'y', 'width', 'fill']; // client i owns prop i; 'fill' is the shared one
    const OWN = [0, 1, 2]; const SHARED = 3; const N_CLIENTS = 3;
    const EDITS = 120, GAP = 100, OFF_START = 3000;
    let seed = 7; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const jit = Array.from({ length: EDITS }, () => ({ up: rnd(), down: [rnd(), rnd(), rnd()] }));
    const pick = Array.from({ length: EDITS }, () => rnd());
    const tj = Array.from({ length: EDITS }, () => rnd());
    function simulate({ whole, keep, delay, overlap, offline }) {
      const edits = Array.from({ length: EDITS }, (_, n) => {
        const client = n % N_CLIENTS;
        const prop = pick[n] < overlap / 100 ? SHARED : OWN[client];
        return { id: n + 1, client, prop, t: n * GAP + Math.floor(tj[n] * 60) };
      });
      const offEnd = OFF_START + offline * 1000;
      const view = Array.from({ length: N_CLIENTS }, () => PROPS.map(() => ({ id: 0, w: -1 })));
      const pend = Array.from({ length: N_CLIENTS }, () => PROPS.map(() => 0));
      const lastSeq = [0, 0, 0];
      const cur = PROPS.map(() => ({ id: 0, w: -1 }));
      let seq = 0, lost = new Set(), lostByReplay = 0, flicker = 0, queued = 0;
      const lastUp = [0, 0, 0], lastDown = [0, 0, 0];
      const ev = []; // {t, k, ...}
      const push = (e) => { let i = ev.length; while (i > 0 && (ev[i - 1].t > e.t || (ev[i-1].t === e.t && ev[i-1].o > e.o))) i--; ev.splice(i, 0, e); };
      const queue = [];
      const isOff = (c, t) => offline > 0 && c === 2 && t >= OFF_START && t < offEnd;
      const send = (e, t, base, snap, replay) => {
        const at = Math.max(lastUp[e.client] + 1, Math.round(t + delay * (0.8 + 0.4 * jit[e.id - 1].up)));
        lastUp[e.client] = at; push({ t: at, o: 1, k: 'arrive', e, base, snap, replay });
      };
      edits.forEach((e) => push({ t: e.t, o: 0, k: 'edit', e }));
      if (offline > 0) push({ t: offEnd, o: 0, k: 'reconnect' });
      while (ev.length) {
        const x = ev.shift();
        if (x.k === 'edit') {
          const e = x.e, c = e.client;
          const base = view[c].map((v) => v.id);
          view[c][e.prop] = { id: e.id, w: c }; pend[c][e.prop]++;
          const snap = view[c].map((v) => ({ ...v }));
          if (isOff(c, x.t)) { queue.push({ e, base, snap }); queued++; }
          else send(e, x.t, base, snap, false);
        } else if (x.k === 'reconnect') {
          view[2] = cur.map((v) => ({ ...v })); pend[2] = PROPS.map(() => 0); lastSeq[2] = seq;
          for (const q of queue) { view[2][q.e.prop] = { id: q.e.id, w: 2 }; pend[2][q.e.prop]++; 
            const base = q.base; const snap = view[2].map(v=>({...v})); send(q.e, x.t, base, snap, true); }
          queue.length = 0;
        } else if (x.k === 'arrive') {
          const { e, base, snap, replay } = x; const c = e.client; seq++;
          const changes = [];
          for (let p = 0; p < PROPS.length; p++) {
            if (!whole && p !== e.prop) continue;
            const next = whole ? snap[p] : { id: e.id, w: c };
            if (next.id === cur[p].id) continue;
            if (cur[p].id !== base[p] && cur[p].w !== c && cur[p].id !== 0) { if (!lost.has(cur[p].id)) { lost.add(cur[p].id); if (replay) lostByReplay++; } }
            cur[p] = { ...next }; changes.push({ p, v: { ...next } });
          }
          for (let d = 0; d < N_CLIENTS; d++) {
            let at = Math.round(x.t + delay * (0.8 + 0.4 * jit[e.id - 1].down[d]));
            at = Math.max(lastDown[d] + 1, at); lastDown[d] = at;
            push({ t: at, o: 2, k: 'deliver', d, seq, src: e, changes });
          }
        } else if (x.k === 'deliver') {
          const { d, seq: s, src, changes } = x;
          if (isOff(d, x.t) || s <= lastSeq[d]) continue;
          lastSeq[d] = s;
          if (src.client === d) pend[d][src.prop] = Math.max(0, pend[d][src.prop] - 1);
          for (const { p, v } of changes) {
            if (pend[d][p] > 0) { if (keep) continue; flicker++; }
            view[d][p] = { ...v };
          }
        }
      }
      const same = view.every((v) => v.every((e, p) => e.id === cur[p].id));
      return { lost: lost.size, flicker, same, queued, lostByReplay, cur, view };
    }

    const NAMES = ['A', 'B', 'C'];
    const rowsEl = q('[data-rows]');
    const tableRows = PROPS.map(() => { const tr = document.createElement('tr'); const cells = Array.from({ length: 5 }, (_, i) => { const c = document.createElement(i === 0 ? 'th' : 'td'); if (i === 0) c.setAttribute('scope', 'row'); tr.append(c); return c; }); rowsEl.append(tr); return cells; });
    const label = (e: any) => (e.id ? `#${e.id} ${NAMES[e.w]}` : 'none');

    function draw() {
      const whole = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-rule]').value === 'whole'; const keep = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-screen]').value === 'keep';
      const delay = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-d]').value); const overlap = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-o]').value); const offline = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-f]').value);
      q('[data-dval]').textContent = `${delay} ms`; q('[data-oval]').textContent = `${overlap}%`; q('[data-fval]').textContent = offline ? `${offline} s` : 'never';
      const r = simulate({ whole, keep, delay, overlap, offline });
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${r.lost} of ${EDITS} edits`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = whole ? 'each edit also puts back old values of the properties its author had not seen change' : 'only an edit to the same property, made without seeing the other one, can be overwritten';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${r.flicker} flickers`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = keep ? 'a screen keeps its own unconfirmed edit and sets aside conflicting server changes' : 'a screen shows every server change as soon as it arrives';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = r.same ? 'all 3 identical' : 'they differ';
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = 'the server\'s order decides the winner, so every copy settles on the same values';
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = r.queued ? `${r.queued} edits replayed` : 'none';
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = r.queued ? `${r.lostByReplay} of the replayed edits overwrote someone else's newer change` : 'Client C stays connected the whole time';
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', r.lost > EDITS / 4 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', r.flicker > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', r.same ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--border)');
      PROPS.forEach((p, i) => {
        const cells = tableRows[i];
        cells[0].textContent = p; cells[1].textContent = label(r.cur[i]);
        for (let c = 0; c < N_CLIENTS; c++) cells[2 + c].textContent = label(r.view[c][i]);
      });
      const out = q('[data-verdict]');
      const bad = (whole && r.lost > 0) || r.flicker > 0 || !r.same;
      out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      let msg: string;
      if (whole) msg = `Each edit sends the whole object, so an edit made before a neighbour's change arrived puts the old values back: ${r.lost} of ${EDITS} edits were overwritten.`;
      else if (r.lost === 0) msg = 'Edits to different properties never conflict, so every edit survived.';
      else msg = `Only edits to the same property conflict. The one that reached the server last won, and ${r.lost} edits were replaced that way.`;
      if (!keep && r.flicker > 0) msg += ` Showing every server change made a screen jump back ${r.flicker} times while its own edit was unconfirmed.`;
      else if (keep) msg += ' No screen flickered.';
      if (r.queued) msg += ` Client C replayed ${r.queued} offline edits on a fresh copy.`;
      out.textContent = msg;
    }
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-rule]').value = 'prop'; q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-screen]').value = 'keep';
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-d]').value = '100'; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-o]').value = '30'; q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-f]').value = '0';
      draw();
    });
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
